KG42.register("rules-a23cb8bd2d8b62dc9d5a76cf",{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R005","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Social-welfare clearing objective","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"The DSO performs social-welfare clearing by solving a welfare maximization problem. Scope: DSO welfare clearing for the distribution feeder. The welfare maximization problem uses a forecast of the feeder's transmission-node TLMP as the marginal cost of serving consumers. Scope: Marginal supply-cost specification in the DSO's distribution-feeder welfare maximization problem.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.social_welfare under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.social_welfare","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.social_welfare","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"DSO welfare clearing for the distribution feeder. | Marginal supply-cost specification in the DSO's distribution-feeder welfare maximization problem.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DSO performs social-welfare clearing by solving a welfare maximization problem. Scope: DSO welfare clearing for the distribution feeder.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The welfare maximization problem uses a forecast of the feeder's transmission-node TLMP as the marginal cost of serving consumers. Scope: Marginal supply-cost specification in the DSO's distribution-feeder welfare maximization problem.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E005","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p02-c1r1__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"PAPAVASILIOU: ANALYSIS OF DISTRIBUTION LOCATIONAL MARGINAL PRICES clearing: (i) aggregators submit d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"(ii) the DSO solves a welfare maximization problem where the marginal cost of power for serving consumers is a forecast of the TLMP of the node at which the distribution feeder is located"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No x objects are declared because the frozen graph contains no variable nodes for the M02 DSO day-ahead welfare maximization problem, and the supplied M02 evidence is prose that gives no mathematical definitions of decision variables or domains. This is not an assertion that the underlying source problem lacks variables; it avoids reusing variables from the separate M03 OPF model.","empty_theta_reason":"No theta objects are declared because the forecast TLMP is mentioned only in prose, without an explicit symbol, indexing domain, unit, numeric value, or parameter definition in the supplied M02 evidence. Importing parameters from the separate M03 radial OPF model would change scope."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.social_welfare","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E005","quote":"the DSO solves a welfare maximization problem"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E005","quote":"the marginal cost of power for serving consumers is a forecast of the TLMP of the node at which the distribution feeder is located"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7fb74f161c1ba9dfaaaeaaf12f1350b18bd840598fe00476cda8df1f9409dbe4","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"This rule is a social-welfare clearing objective, so it is not merely procedural. However, the only supplied same-rule evidence, v141-b-g01-E005 (unreviewed), is introductory prose: it states that the DSO solves a welfare maximization problem and that the marginal cost of serving consumers is a forecast of the feeder's transmission-node TLMP. It does not supply an objective function, decision variables, constraints, domains, units, numerical values, or a source-defined mathematical notation for the M02 DSO clearing problem. The frozen graph contains only clearing.social_welfare and coordination.local_operator, with no variable or parameter nodes. The paper does contain welfare formulations (I) and (II), but those belong to the separate M03 radial OPF/DLMP analysis and use consumer-benefit and generator-cost terms rather than the M02 forecast-TLMP marginal supply cost. Importing those variables or formulas would change scope. Therefore no supported formal expression can be produced for this rule without graph revision and/or source re-extraction.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R005-E001"],"rationale":"C001 states that the DSO, represented by coordination.local_operator, performs social-welfare clearing, represented by clearing.social_welfare. The frozen graph represents this relation with edge v141-c-R005-E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","node_ids":["clearing.social_welfare"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 specifies the marginal supply cost used inside the social-welfare clearing objective, so it is attached to clearing.social_welfare. The frozen graph has no parameter node for a forecast TLMP and no edge representing this internal cost specification."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: If this rule is to be formalized, add or identify graph object nodes for the decision variables of the M02 DSO day-ahead welfare maximization, such as served consumer demand or consumption quantities and any relevant generation or bid quantities, with source-grounded definitions and domains. Do not reuse M03 variables such as p_i^c, p_i^g, f_i^p, f_i^q, l_i, or v_i unless the source explicitly places them in this M02 clearing problem.","C.1: Add or identify a parameter node for the forecast TLMP at the transmission node where the distribution feeder is located, including its role as the marginal cost of serving consumers and any source-defined index or unit; alternatively confirm that the frozen graph intentionally represents only the prose relationship.","B re-extraction: Obtain the exact same-scope Li et al. [12] day-ahead DSO welfare program, or another exact source equation for this M02 DSO welfare clearing problem, including objective function, decision variables, constraints, and the forecast-TLMP marginal-cost treatment. Current candidate evidence v141-b-g01-E005 is unreviewed introductory prose and is insufficient to support a formal expression."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
